  },
  {
   "id": "common-mistakes",
   "heading": "Common mistakes",
   "role": "depth",
   "steps": [
    {
     "id": "common-mistakes-1",
     "blocks": [
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Forgetting the real rate.** The IS curve uses $i_t - \\pi_t$; raising $i$ by less than $\\pi$ loosens policy.\n- **Reading θ backwards.** A *larger* $\\beta_\\pi$ means a *smaller* θ: inflation responds less, output more.\n- **Expectations timing.** Adaptive means $\\pi^e_t = \\pi_{t-1}$: last period's inflation, not next period's."
      }
     ],
     "words": 39,
     "symbols": [
      "$\\pi_t$",
      "$\\pi^e_t$",
      "$i_t$",
      "$\\beta_\\pi$"
     ]
    }
